// DB-1 (MAIN project) rules for the new system  ->  Firebase Console -> Firestore Database -> Rules -> Publish
//
// Phones / the user app never touch Firestore any more (everything goes through the load balancer), so normal users get NOTHING here.
// The ADMIN panel pages (admin.html: users, finance, matches, gift codes, leaderboard ...) sign in with a custom token that carries
// the claim  admin: true  and read / write Firestore straight from the browser, so they MUST be allowed here.
// Servers (S1-S5), the Payment Bot and the Backup Center use the Admin SDK and ignore these rules.
//
// Publish this ONLY AFTER the new user app is live (older cached app versions that talk to Firestore directly stop working).
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {
    function isAdmin() { return request.auth != null && request.auth.token.admin == true; }
    match /{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if isAdmin();
    }
  }
}
